    "final_text": "I added `updateQuantity(name, quantity)` to `ShoppingCart` in `src/cart.js`, and the full suite passes (41 tests, 7 of them new).\n\n- **Validation:** it checks the quantity and that the item exists before changing anything, so a rejected call leaves the cart as it was.\n- **Behaviour:** a positive integer sets the quantity, and 0 removes the item.\n- **Errors:** a negative or non-integer quantity throws a `RangeError`, which matches `addItem`. A missing item throws a plain `Error`.\n- **Tests:** the new `updateQuantity` block in `tests/cart.test.js` covers these cases:\n  - increasing and decreasing an item's quantity\n  - removal at 0\n  - negative, fractional, NaN, Infinity, string, `undefined` and `null` quantities\n  - an item that isn't in the cart, and an empty cart\n  - the cart being unchanged after each rejected call\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
